  "rule": "TextPaths: a glyph's quad runs advance along its tangent (cos a, sin a) from its origin, from descent below to ascent above, up = (sin a, -cos a), a clockwise in degrees; corners top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left. A curve's band is the annular sector round centre from r-descent-pad to r+ascent+pad (r signed), over angles from..to (radians, clockwise from up; a point at angle a and radius R is centre + R(sin a, -cos a)), extended pad/|r| each way; a radius of the other sign to r is the centre. A path's band is the strip from descent+pad below to ascent+pad above the baseline, from-pad to to+pad along it, offset at both ends and every vertex between by the heading of the segment it ends. A column's band is its cells' box grown by pad. pad = 0.18 x fontSize x spread / 50; corners round by roundness/100 of half the thickness (ascent+descent+2pad). Bounds are [x, y, w, h].",
